 ## Operating characteristics
--   **Time Complexity:** The inject pass is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of froxels (one thread per column). The blur pass is $O(K)$ where $K$ is the number of revealed froxels. In the worst case (camera cut), $K$ equals the total number of froxels. In typical frames, $K$ is small [S2, unofficial].
+-   **Time Complexity:** The inject pass is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of froxels (one thread per column) [S2, unofficial]. The blur pass is $O(K)$ where $K$ is the number of revealed froxels [S2, unofficial]. In the worst case (camera cut), $K$ equals the total number of froxels [S2, unofficial]. In typical frames, $K$ is small [S2, unofficial].
 -   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ for the froxel volumes and the revealed froxel list buffer [S2, unofficial].
--   **Measured Performance:** A frame where nothing was revealed costs a single-thread pass and two empty indirect dispatches. A camera cut costs a blur over most of the grid [S2, unofficial].
--   **Strengths:** Reduces noise in revealed froxels without blurring converged history. Cost is proportional to the number of revealed froxels.
--   **Limitations:** Does not fix the root cause of revealed froxel noise (lack of shadow history). Relies on static shadow maps (no moving sun/occluder). Anisotropic blur due to exponential slice spacing.
